{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-18282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ if its determinant is $-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-18282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(3-0) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21}=\\frac{1}{-2}\\cdot (-3)=\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-18282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ac7cf98f9f7eaad6b9fdd30be032102f8ca59befb4a38c9a4d0f89d152fe5257"} {"question" "q-18282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-18282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-18282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-18285" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-18285" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-0+(0-2) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{13}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{13} & =(-1)^{1+3}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-2 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{31}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13}=\\frac{1}{-2}\\cdot (-2)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-18285" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ac7cf98f9f7eaad6b9fdd30be032102f8ca59befb4a38c9a4d0f89d152fe5257"} {"question" "q-18285" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-18285" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-18285" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-104431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & k \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $-1$ and $det(A)=4-2k.$ Find the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-104431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=4-2k\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2-0) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-2k}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{32}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{k-2} & =-1 \\\\ 1 & =2-k \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-104431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ac7cf98f9f7eaad6b9fdd30be032102f8ca59befb4a38c9a4d0f89d152fe5257"} {"question" "q-104431" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-104431" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-104431" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-319443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & k & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $det(A)=k-2.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-319443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=k-2\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{13}^{t}={c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}k & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}k & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(k-2)}\\cdot (k+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{k+2}{\\,k-2\\,}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{13}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k+2}{\\,k-2\\,} & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2(k+2) & =-(k-2) \\\\ 2k+4 & =-k+2 \\\\ 3k & =-2 \\\\ k & =-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-319443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ac7cf98f9f7eaad6b9fdd30be032102f8ca59befb4a38c9a4d0f89d152fe5257"} {"question" "q-319443" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-319443" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-319937" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & k & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nequals $-1.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-319937" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & k & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ k & -2\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(1\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot k)+(0\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot 3)+(0\\cdot k-1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =2(k-2)+3-3 \\\\  & =2k-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}^{t}={c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-(-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{23}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2k-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{23}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{k-2} & =-1 \\\\ 1 & =-(k-2) \\\\ k-2 & =-1 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-319937" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ac7cf98f9f7eaad6b9fdd30be032102f8ca59befb4a38c9a4d0f89d152fe5257"} {"question" "q-319937" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"} {"question" "q-319937" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "1da5000239ac6a483ed36bee8d5e200c3d973d6d1d48173067593caafeaaf6b8"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1016 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
